ACL / ARR Paper (typage/acl) - license

This template contains files from two sources.

  main.tex, refs.bib, manifest.json, typage.json, LICENSE
      Written by 7D24H. CC0-1.0: dedicated to the public domain; papers
      written from this template need no attribution.
      https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

  acl.sty, acl_natbib.bst
      The official style files of the Association for Computational
      Linguistics, from https://github.com/acl-org/acl-style-files (commit
      d5adc823ff0f80f98c80405ca0ab66c68e684409).
      acl.sty carries no license statement (rights remain with the ACL and
      the authors named in the file). acl_natbib.bst (modifications by Norman
      Gray, based on natbib's styles by Patrick W Daly) is under the LaTeX
      Project Public License, as stated in its header. Both files are
      redistributed unmodified, so that the template compiles offline.

The packages the sample loads (times, inconsolata, natbib, ...) come from
the built-in Tectonic bundle under their own licenses. Check the current
call for papers and https://acl-org.github.io/ACLPUB/ for the rules that
apply to your submission.
